# How much did the first hard drive weigh?
subtitle: "Guess how much the first hard drive weighed in 1956, then compare it with the microSD card in your phone, a gram that holds a terabyte."

## How much did the first hard drive weigh?
affirm: playful
text: {"font_size":34}
sources:
    - id: ibm350
      title: IBM 350
      authors: Wikipedia
      year: 2025
      url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IBM_350
      finding: 5 million 6-bit characters (3.75 MB) on fifty 24-inch disks at 1,200 rpm; cabinet 152 cm long, 172 cm high, 74 cm wide; the RAMAC 305 system leased for $3,200 a month
    - id: thelen
      title: Myths about IBM RAMAC, the first HDD
      authors: E. Thelen
      year: 2015
      url: https://ed-thelen.org/RAMAC/Myths.html
      finding: the IBM 350 weighed 1,730 lb (785 kg); 'over a ton' figures include the separate air compressor

    path cab closed #5e584e points [[55,290],[347,290],[347,620],[55,620]] style.fill #c9c2b4 style.fill_style wash style.stroke_width 4 hidden true
    path win closed #5e584e points [[105,360],[297,360],[297,590],[105,590]] style.stroke_width 2 hidden true
    path d0 #5e584e points [[115,380],[287,380]] style.stroke_width 2 hidden true
