    card title "How much did the first hard drive weigh?"

In 1956, IBM shipped the first hard drive, a cabinet as tall as a person. It held five million characters, about three and three-quarter megabytes.
    group cabinet members ["cab","win","d0","d1","d2","d3","d4","d5","d6","d7"]
    text name "IBM 350, 1956" x 680 y 620 font_size 46
    text cap "3.75 MB" #2f6b8f cites ["ibm350"] x 680 y 540 font_size 46

That is about one photo on your phone today.
    scale kg cites ["thelen"] x 60 y 225 width 880 unit kg min 0.0001 max 10000 value 800 log true

    ask "How many kilograms did the first hard drive weigh? Click on the line." on kg store w default "10"
        right: Close: you said {w}, and it was about {w.true}.
        wrong: You said {w}; it was about {w.true}.

Nearly a tonne, as heavy as a small car. It was moved with forklifts, and flown in cargo planes.
    text ton "nearly a tonne" #b5482e cites ["thelen"] x 680 y 445 font_size 50
    icon car size 110 set twemoji x 680 y 355 icon_look picture of automobile

    erase ton car

Inside, fifty metal disks, each sixty-one centimetres across, spun twelve hundred times a minute.
    text platters "50 disks, 61 cm" #2f6b8f x 680 y 445 font_size 46

    erase platters

And you could not buy one. Companies rented the whole system, for about three thousand two hundred dollars a month.
    text rent "$3,200 a month" #2f6b8f x 680 y 445 font_size 46

    erase rent

Now draw a microSD card at the same scale. It is this speck, and it weighs under a gram.
    path sd closed thick #b5482e points [[398,290],[404,290],[404,294],[398,294]] style.fill #b5482e style.fill_style wash
    arrow sd_arrow #b5482e from.x 510 from.y 335 to.x 408 to.y 296
    text sd_l "microSD" #b5482e x 560 y 355 font_size 40

Yet a one-terabyte card holds more than a quarter of a million times as much.
    text tb "1 TB, under 1 g" #b5482e x 680 y 445 font_size 46

Megabyte for megabyte, today's card is hundreds of billions of times lighter.
    point at.ref sd_l gesture underline

